<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cunipert</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 700</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Cunincpert</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cunipert was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-the-lombards">King of the Lombards</a>, co-ruler with his father Perctarit from 680 and sole king from 688 to 700. Early in his reign the rebel duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alahis">Alahis</a> seized Pavia, but Cunipert defeated and killed him at Coronate in 689. His reign was otherwise peaceful; at a synod in Pavia in 698 he helped end the Three Chapters schism in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cunipert.jpg" alt="Cunipert" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cunincpert_tremissis_612190.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
